# Keep skills and subagents up to date

When you change the project in ways that affect how agents should work, update the matching skill and subagent so future agents stay accurate.

## When to update

- **New major component or directory** (e.g. new `pkg/` package, new `cmd/` tool): Add or extend the relevant skill in `.cursor/skills/` and, if it deserves focused multi-step work, add a subagent in `.cursor/agents/` with the same name and aligned description/scope.
- **API, auth, store, WebUI, or server job changes**: Update `.cursor/skills/gsbs-server/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/gsbs-server.md` (routes, store methods, conventions, checklist).
- **Client sync, config, watcher, tray, or list changes**: Update `.cursor/skills/gsbs-client/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/gsbs-client.md` (config shape, folder-exists rule, manifest usage).
- **PCGW, path resolution, or manifest schema changes**: Update `.cursor/skills/gsbs-pcgw-paths/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/gsbs-pcgw-paths.md` (placeholders, resolver, rate limits, DB columns).
- **Build, release, or Docker changes**: Update `.cursor/skills/gsbs-release/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/gsbs-release.md` (ldflags, script, env, docs).
- **Architecture or plan changes**: Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and, if delegation or scoping changes, `.cursor/SUBAGENTS.md` and `AGENTS.md`.

## How to update

- **Skills** (`.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`): Keep scope, conventions, and checklists accurate. Preserve frontmatter `name` and `description`; refine `description` if the “when to use” trigger changes.
- **Subagents** (`.cursor/agents/<name>.md`): Keep the prompt body and scope in sync with the skill. Ensure frontmatter `description` matches when the agent should delegate (e.g. “Use when…” / “Use proactively for…”). Same names as skills (gsbs-server, gsbs-client, gsbs-pcgw-paths, gsbs-release) so the mapping stays 1:1.
- **SUBAGENTS.md**: Keep the “When to use which skill” table and role summaries aligned with actual skills and subagents. Add a row or role if you add a new skill/subagent pair.

## One-to-one mapping

Each domain has one skill and one subagent with the same name: gsbs-server, gsbs-client, gsbs-pcgw-paths, gsbs-release. When you edit one, consider whether the other needs the same scope/convention update so they stay consistent.
